<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q#9-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain how you know. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
    <list>
      <item>Inequality 1 shows the pay at the hotel \( (18h+33) \) being greater than the pay at the restaurant \( 7.50h+ \frac{50}{4} \). Earlier, we found out that the hotel job is better when the student works less than 16.5 hours. Graph B shows \( h&lt;16.5 \). This means Graph B shows the solution to Inequality 1.</item>
      <item>If we substitute a value greater than 16.5 for \( h \), we have a true statement for Inequality 2 and a false statement for Inequality 1. This means \( h&gt;16.5 \) is a solution to Inequality 2 but not to Inequality 1. </item>
      <item>If we substitute a value less than 16.5 for \( h \), we have a true statement for Inequality 1 but not for Inequality 2. So \( h&lt;16.5 \) is a solution to Inequality 1.</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL --></section>
